{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Let there be lights.</b> It is the way of verses to speak in singular form concerning a plural, such as 'ויהי אנשים אשר היו טמאים' (there were men who were impure). And so it explains 'let there be lights.' And what are the lights? <b>Lights</b> — the light that was born from the light created on the first day, He divided into two pieces, one larger than the other; they are the sun and the moon. And what He wrote, 'and the stars,' is stated in the doing (עשיה) and not stated in the command (צוואה), to teach that when the one light was divided into two, sparks flew off from it, and from these were the stars." "<b>Lights.</b> Defective spelling (חסר, written without the vav), because it was not created to illuminate except the sphere of the sun alone, and the moon was created to count seasons." "<b>In the firmament of the heavens.</b> In the firmament that is spread out and stretched beneath the upper heavens." "<b>To divide between the day and between the night.</b> The sun separates from it the night that has passed, and the moon separates from it the day that has passed." "<b>And they shall be for signs.</b> Through them I shall make signs, such as for Moses, for Joshua, and for Hezekiah, and as it is written: 'מאותות השמים אל תחתו' (of the signs of the heavens do not be dismayed). Another interpretation: <b>and they shall be for signs</b> — concerning future events, for diviners tell future events based on what they see in them." "<b>And for the seasons.</b> That are reckoned from the moon: Rosh Chodesh, the fifteenth of Nisan, the sixth of Sivan, the first of Tishrei, the tenth of Tishrei, the fifteenth of Tishrei. And so David said: ״עשה ירח למועדים״ (He made the moon for the seasons)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:19:17.695676565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}